13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T06:28:22Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-07-04T19:42:30Z","updated_at":"2026-08-24T19:51:16Z","closed_at":"2026-08-24T19:51:16Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.7.stable\n\n### System information\n\nWindwos 11 Godot 4.7 stable forward+ rx6650XT ryzen5 5600\n\n### Issue description\n\nGodot 4.7 introduced a global search/filter feature for `PopupMenu` nodes across the editor. However, the popup menu used to select and add animations inside an `AnimationTree` (specifically when right-clicking in an AnimationNodeStateMachine or BlendTree graph and hovering over **Add Animation**) does not benefit from this new feature.\n\nWhen working with complex skeletons or large animation sets (like ALS ports), the list is massive and desperately needs the new 4.7 popup search bar to be usable.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Use Godot 4.7 (dev/beta) and create a project with a large number of animations.\n2. Setup an `AnimationTree` with an `AnimationNodeStateMachine`.\n3. Open the AnimationTree editor panel.\n4. Right-click the graph, hover over **Add Animation**.\n5. Notice that the animation selection submenu does not include the new 4.7 search bar/filter mechanism, unlike other updated menus in this version.\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A (UI/UX issue visible in any project with multiple animations)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","followi